s, volumetric mist, aggressive handheld energy, sharp impact timing, speed-ramps on jumps, and natural motion blur. Use predominantly medium and medium-full compositions so the full-body motion stays visible, while keeping <Subject 1>'s face readable in 3/4 or frontal angles during movement. Avoid distant wide shots that shrink the subject. Keep the action intense but non-graphic: no gore, no blood, no text overlays beyond diegetic signage, no logos, no watermarks.\n\n[Shot 1] At 00:00.000, the video opens with a medium-full 50mm fast side-tracking shot, framed from the chunky sneakers to the top of the pink cap. <Subject 1> sprints at full speed down a rain-slicked neon alley, weaving past holographic kanji signs and low-hanging pipes. The camera tracks laterally at sprint pace with a slight forward push. Her pink hair streams behind her, the hoodie flaps, and chunky sneakers splash through puddles. Her face is visible in 3/4 view as she glances toward the camera mid-stride. A hard musical hit and a burst of rain spray open the sequence.\n\n[Shot 2] At 00:01.800, cut to a medium 35mm low-angle handheld chase shot from front-low. <Subject 1> launches into a parkour vault over a waist-high neon railing, legs splitting cleanly in the air. Use a brief speed-ramp into near slow-motion at the vault apex — her face fully visible to camera — then snap back to real speed on impact. Add a whip pan and a controlled camera jolt as she lands and immediately accelerates. Keep her face, cap, and hoodie graffiti readable through the entire vault.\n\n[Shot 3] At 00:04.000, use a medium-full 40mm shot with the camera tilting sharply upward. <Subject 1> takes two running steps up a vertical neon-lit wall and pushes off into a twisting jump. Crash-zoom to her face at the top of the wall-run — the key face-coherence moment, magenta neon washing across her cheek from the side. She lands with a splash on the wet rooftop below, rolling through the impact.\n\n[Shot 4] At 00:06.300, cut to a medium 50mm shot. <Subject 1> sprints and leaps across a wide gap between two rooftops, holographic advertisements streaking through the fog below. Heavy speed-ramp: near slow-motion at the jump apex with her hair, hoodie, and cap all airborne, face fully frontal to the camera — then fast on the descent. She lands into a shoulder roll. Keep the pink face mark under her eye and her dark eye makeup coherent and unsmeared through the slow-motion segment.\n\n[Shot 5] At 00:08.300, cut to an 85mm close-up of <Subject 1>'s face and shoulders. She rises out of the roll into a low crouch, lifts her chin, and stares directly into the camera with a confident street-hero expression. Magenta neon rim light behind her, cyan key light from the front, rain droplets clinging to her hair and cap. Hold the final close-up for the last 0.3 seconds, ending exactly at 00:10.000.\n\noverall_soundscape:\nFast wet footsteps, heavy controlled breathing, fabric and chain whipping in the wind, the slap of palms on wall, vault launch and landing thuds, puddle splashes on impact, distant city bass, neon sign buzz, and a rising siren. Add controlled low-frequency impact hits synchronized with each vault and landing. No spoken dialogue.\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\nA high-energy cyberpunk drum-and-bass score at approximately 140 BPM, with driving breakbeat drums, distorted reese bass, agitated synth arpeggios, metallic percussion, and sub-bass impacts synced to each vault and jump. Energy climbs through [Shot 2], peaks on the rooftop leap in [Shot 4] with a rising brass-and-synth swell, then cuts to a single sustained magenta synth stab under the final hero close-up.", 1344, 768, 124, "match"], "inputs": [{"name": "clip", "link": 272, "label": "clip", "type": "CLIP", "localized_name": "clip"}, {"name": "vae", "link": 420, "label": "vae", "type": "VAE", "localized_name": "vae"}, {"name": "audio_vae", "link": 425, "label": "audio_vae", "type": "VAE", "localized_name": "audio_vae"}, {"shape": 7, "name":